#
# spr_limit.checks - one row per CHECK of fixtures/src/spr_limit.s (D-125, plan 04.1-02). Columns separated by one TAB: check index (1-based), slug, class tag, meaning.
# Class tags: MAN:<page> (a manual page value; the page label must be in fixtures/lib/cites.txt), GUEST:<model>, ASSUMED:<LED-id>.
# Checks 1 and 2 are readbacks of what the guest wrote against an additive sum (the palette), so they hold under every power-on policy (D-167). Checks 3 to 8 are the status byte the guest reads after one clean frame of each sprite scene (the SATB is written first and copied by DMA before the sprites are switched on, so the byte does not depend on the power-on content).
# Classes (ER-10, review fixes H-01 and M-01 of the Phase 4.1 review): check 3 (16 sprites, 16 slots, no OR) is MAN H7-19 and check 7 (CR set) is MAN H7-4 (CR is sprite 0 against another sprite; a flag is set when its enable is set). Check 4 is ASSUMED LED-VID-0012: OR with only 16 covering sprites rests on the 12-slot reading of one 16-wide sprite
# as one slot and on the model reading that a dropped sprite sets OR (both pages put the OR threshold at 17 or more). Check 6 (the 17 point) is ASSUMED LED-VID-0012, the disagreement of H7-4 and H7-19. Checks 5 and 8 are ASSUMED LED-VID-0008: they assert that a flag whose enable is clear stays clear (check 5: OR alone on a line where sprite 0 and sprite 1
# are both opaque at the dots 14 and 15 with the CR enable clear; check 8: no CR flag with its enable clear), the converse that LED-VID-0008 records as the reading of three emulators. VD dependence (a recorded limit): every status byte here also asserts bit 5 (VD) = 0 after a VBlank with CR bit 3 clear, the same converse; checks 3 and 7 keep MAN for the
# flag they judge. The raster, the slot counts, the dropped sprites and the flags of the records are judged from the line records by the video case (fixtures/src/spr_limit.vexp). A pass is not a support claim (ER-4).
id=26
checks=8
1	pal-low-sum	GUEST:pal-bijection	The 512 palette entry low bytes equal the additive running sum E(i + 1) = (E(i) + 91) & 511 from E(0) = 17, a different computation from the multiplicative writer
2	pal-bit8-sum	GUEST:pal-bijection	The 512 palette entry bit 8 values equal the same running sum
3	or-clear-16	MAN:H7-19	16 sprites cover one line with 16 slots (HDE 3, e = 10): no OR flag, the status read after a clean frame is $00
4	or-set-e8	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0012	The same 16 sprites with HDE 1 (e = 8, 2 * (8 - 2) = 12 slots): four are dropped and OR (bit 1) is set alone
5	or-set-18	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0008	18 sprites cover one line with 16 slots: OR is set, bit 1 alone
6	or-set-17	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0012	17 sprites cover one line with HDE 5 (e = 12: 20 slots by the formula, the cap of 16 binds): the model sets OR (H7-19 says 17 or more, H7-4 says more than 17), bit 1 alone
7	cr-set	MAN:H7-4	Sprite 0 opaque over another sprite with CR bit 0 set: the CR flag, bit 0, alone
8	cr-gated	ASSUMED:LED-VID-0008	The same scene with CR bit 0 clear: the flag is not set and the status read is $00
